        {
          "question": "q-98524",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t),\\,{f}_{3}(t)=t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[0,\\pi ]$ of continuous functions over $[0,\\pi ]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}_{1}(t)\u22a5{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- ${f}_{1}(t)\u22a5{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- $S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070949/state.json",
