          "reviewer_session": "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca",
          "rationale": "For the original functions and integration interval [0,pi], the inner product of cos(t) and sin(2t) is (1/2) integral_0^pi [sin(t)+sin(3t)] dt = 4/3, so statement I is false. The inner product of cos(t) and t is [t sin(t)+cos(t)]_0^pi = -2, so statement II is false. Since these pairs are not orthogonal, the set is not orthogonal and statement III is false. Thus original option a, index 0, is uniquely correct. This derivation agrees with the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grading; it contradicts the stored 'II only' key.",
